$ rgit tip 1
Tip 1 of 36: Undo almost anything

  `rgit undo` takes back the last command that changed the repository: a
  commit, reset, rebase, merge or deleted branch. `rgit redo` brings it back.

  Try: rgit undo --list
$ rgit bingo 7
Tip 7 of 36: Uncommit

  `rgit reset --soft HEAD~1` takes the last commit off the branch and leaves
  its changes staged, ready to commit again (`rgit commit -C ORIG_HEAD` keeps
  the message).

  Try: rgit reset --soft HEAD~1
$ rgit tip --all
  1  Undo almost anything
  2  Ask what went wrong
  3  One screen on where you are
  4  Three trees
  5  Stage part of a file
  6  Unstage without losing anything
  7  Uncommit
  8  Fix an older commit
